          "distinct": false,
          "id": "57b63bca2e470d17eec38533a81c6fdd2a389a1c",
          "message": "Update module github.com/shirou/gopsutil/v4 to v4.26.10 (#16295)\n\nThis PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change |\n[Age](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n[Confidence](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|\n[github.com/shirou/gopsutil/v4](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil)\n| `v4.26.9` → `v4.26.10` |\n![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/go/github.com%2fshirou%2fgopsutil%2fv4/v4.26.10?slim=true)\n|\n![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/go/github.com%2fshirou%2fgopsutil%2fv4/v4.26.9/v4.26.10?slim=true)\n|\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>shirou/gopsutil (github.com/shirou/gopsutil/v4)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v4.26.10`](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/releases/tag/v4.26.10)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/compare/v4.26.9...v4.26.10)\n\n<!-- Release notes generated using configuration in .github/release.yml\nat v4.26.10 -->\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> ## Planned breaking change: `disk.IOCounters` `ReadTime` / `WriteTime`\non Windows\n>\n> This release includes\n[#&#8203;2164](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/issues/2164).\nIn a future release, the Windows values of ReadTime and WriteTime will\nchange significantly (seconds to milliseconds). The API will not change.\n>\n> On Windows, `ReadTime` and `WriteTime` are currently in **seconds**.\n> On Linux, macOS and FreeBSD they are in **milliseconds**.\n> This is a bug\n([#&#8203;2160](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/issues/2160)).\n>\n> - **In a future release, the default on Windows will change to\nmilliseconds.**\n> - This will happen when psutil fixes the same bug\n([giampaolo/psutil#3002](https://redirect.github.com/giampaolo/psutil/issues/3002)),\nor in **February 2027** at the latest.\n> - After that change, Windows values will be 1000x larger than now.\n>\n> You can switch to milliseconds now with the new context key\n`disk.WillBeDeletedOptInWindowsIOTimeMs`:\n>\n> ```go\n> ctx := context.WithValue(context.Background(),\ndisk.WillBeDeletedOptInWindowsIOTimeMs, true)\n> stats, err := disk.IOCountersWithContext(ctx)\n> ```\n>\n> - Without this key, nothing changes in this release.\n> - Other platforms ignore this key.\n> - This key will be removed when milliseconds become the default.\n>   Remove it from your code at that time.\n>\n>\n([#&#8203;2164](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/issues/2164))\n\n##### What's Changed\n\n##### disk\n\n- disk/windows: convert IOCounters Read/WriteTime to milliseconds by\n[@&#8203;TastyHeadphones](https://redirect.github.com/TastyHeadphones)\nin [#&#8203;2164](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/pull/2164)\n\n##### host\n\n- \\[host]\\[linux]: fix loginctl users fallback for systemd >= 256 by\n[@&#8203;houssemexo26](https://redirect.github.com/houssemexo26) in\n[#&#8203;2168](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/pull/2168)\n- \\[host]\\[linux]: Fall back to loginctl when utmp is unavailable by\n[@&#8203;SebastianLeitz](https://redirect.github.com/SebastianLeitz) in\n[#&#8203;2132](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/pull/2132)\n- \\[sensors]\\[freebsd]: implement TemperaturesWithContext by\n[@&#8203;AdamMagued](https://redirect.github.com/AdamMagued) in\n[#&#8203;2173](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/pull/2173)\n\n##### mem\n\n- Compute swap used as total minus free on AIX by\n[@&#8203;pgimalac](https://redirect.github.com/pgimalac) in\n[#&#8203;2166](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/pull/2166)\n\n##### process\n\n- process: keep /dev/tty\\* when /dev/pts is missing by\n[@&#8203;TastyHeadphones](https://redirect.github.com/TastyHeadphones)\nin [#&#8203;2167](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/pull/2167)\n\n##### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;TastyHeadphones](https://redirect.github.com/TastyHeadphones)\nmade their first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2167](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/pull/2167)\n- [@&#8203;houssemexo26](https://redirect.github.com/houssemexo26) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2168](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/pull/2168)\n- [@&#8203;SebastianLeitz](https://redirect.github.com/SebastianLeitz)\nmade their first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2132](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/pull/2132)\n- [@&#8203;AdamMagued](https://redirect.github.com/AdamMagued) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2173](https://redirect.github.com/shirou/gopsutil/pull/2173)\n\n**Full Changelog**:\n<https://github.com/shirou/gopsutil/compare/v4.26.9...v4.26.10>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Configuration\n\n📅 **Schedule**: (UTC)\n\n- Branch creation\n  - \"on tuesday\"\n- Automerge\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n\n🚦 **Automerge**: Disabled by config. Please merge this manually once you\nare satisfied.\n\n♻ **Rebasing**: Whenever PR becomes conflicted, or you tick the\nrebase/retry checkbox.\n\n🔕 **Ignore**: Close this PR and you won't be reminded about this update\nagain.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check\nthis box\n\n---\n\nThis PR was generated by [Mend Renovate](https://mend.io/renovate/).\nView the [repository job\nlog](https://developer.mend.io/github/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector).\n\n<!--renovate-debug:eyJjcmVhdGVkSW5WZXIiOiI0NC4yMDIuMSIsInVwZGF0ZWRJblZlciI6IjQ0LjIwMi4xIiwidGFyZ2V0QnJhbmNoIjoibWFpbiIsImxhYmVscyI6WyJkZXBlbmRlbmNpZXMiLCJyZW5vdmF0ZWJvdCJdfQ==-->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: otelbot <197425009+otelbot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Alex Boten <223565+codeboten@users.noreply.github.com>",
