          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2583302d78e19c4cf7fda45b664ea55cdf39a735",
          "message": "[config/confighttp, config/configgrpc] Bound the zstd decoder window by the server's size limit (#16281)\n\n#### Description\n\nSmall degenerate zstd payloads can cause disproportionate memory\nallocation, resulting in denial of service when zstd compression is used\nin the OTLP grpc and http receivers.\n\nThe decoder allocates the window a frame declares before it produces any\noutput, and the library default permits windows up to 512 MiB. Both\ncollector decompression paths let a request drive that allocation before\n`max_request_body_size` or `max_recv_msg_size_mib` applies, because\nthose bound the decoded output, not the window. On gRPC the message is\ndecompressed in the transport ahead of any interceptor, so a receiver\nthat requires a header still allocates for a request it will reject.\n\nThis bounds the window by what each server already accepts: HTTP derives\nit from `max_request_body_size`, gRPC from `max_recv_msg_size_mib` via\n`zstd.SetMaxRecvMsgSize`. Neither bound goes below 8 MiB, the largest\nwindow a default-configured encoder declares, so frames from default\nencoders keep decoding. `decoderWrapper` also implements `io.Closer`, so\ngRPC returns a decoder to its pool as soon as it is done with a message\ninstead of leaving it to the finalizer.\n\n#### Link to tracking issue\nFixes #16280; related to open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification#5321\nand Honeycomb internal issue SECENG-963\n\n#### Testing\n\nNew tests in both packages: a crafted frame declaring a 512 MiB window\nis rejected with bounded allocation, a payload from a default-configured\nencoder still decodes, and an early-stopped gRPC read releases its\ndecoder. Both rejection tests fail without the fix. `go test -race`\npasses for `config/confighttp` and `config/configgrpc`, `golangci-lint`\nis clean for both modules, and `make chlog-validate` passes.\n\n#### Documentation\n\nNo configuration or API changes for users, so no documentation update.\n\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-03T23:45:32Z",
