          "id": "79bf8a49d2e4556e3aa72ac36e3b1e460a176ac1",
          "message": "[chore] clean up makefile warnings (#16312)\n\n#### Description\n\nSince making internal/statusutil into its own module, been seeing\nwarnings when running make commands in this repo. This cleans those up\n\nbefore:\n```\n$ make gobenchmark\ngo: warning: \"./...\" matched no packages\ngo: warning: \"./...\" matched no packages\ngo: warning: \"./...\" matched no packages\ngo: warning: \"./...\" matched no packages\ngo: warning: \"./...\" matched no packages\ngo: warning: \"./...\" matched no packages\nRunning target 'benchmark' in module 'client'\n```\n\nafter:\n\n```\n$ make gobenchmark \nRunning target 'benchmark' in module 'client'\n/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/make -C client benchmark\nMEMBENCH=yes go tool -modfile /Users/alexboten/dev/opentelemetry-collector/internal/tools/go.mod gotestsum \\\n                --packages=\"go.opentelemetry.io/collector/client\" -- \\\n                -bench=. -run=notests ./... | tee benchmark.txt\n```\n<!--Ex. Fixing a bug - Describe the bug and how this fixes the issue.\nEx. Adding a feature - Explain what this achieves.-->\n\n\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\nSigned-off-by: Alex Boten <223565+codeboten@users.noreply.github.com>",
