          "distinct": false,
          "id": "9b35cca53b62b282a2fb42eba971d150533ccddc",
          "message": "[pkg/xreceiverhelper] Report profile sample metrics per sample type (#16251)\n\n<!--Ex. Fixing a bug - Describe the bug and how this fixes the issue.\nEx. Adding a feature - Explain what this achieves.-->\n#### Description\nAdd `ObsReport.EndProfilesOpBySampleType` and\n`ProfileSampleCountsByType` so\n`otelcol_receiver_{accepted,refused,failed}_profile_samples` can carry a\n`sample_type` attribute. Use it in the OTLP receiver.\n\nA single OTLP profiles payload can hold several profiles with different\nsample types, e.g. CPU samples, off-CPU time and allocations. A plain\nsample count adds all of them together. It can't show which kind of\nprofile data was accepted or lost, and it mixes samples whose values\nmean different things (e.g. \"samples:count\" vs \"off_cpu:nanoseconds\").\nTagging the counters with the sample type, as \"type:unit\", shows which\nprofile types were affected by refused or failed requests. It also shows\nhow much of each type the receiver ingests.\n\n<!-- Issue number if applicable -->\n#### Link to tracking issue\nFixes #\n\n<!--Describe what testing was performed and which tests were added.-->\n#### Testing\n\n<!--Describe the documentation added.-->\n#### Documentation\n\n<!--Authorship attestation. See AGENTS.md for details. AI agents must\nnot check this box on behalf\nof the user; the human author must check it themselves before the PR is\nready for review.-->\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n<!--Please delete paragraphs that you did not use before submitting.-->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florian Lehner <florian.lehner@datadoghq.com>\nCo-authored-by: Yang Song <songy23@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Damien Mathieu <42@dmathieu.com>\nCo-authored-by: Alex Boten <223565+codeboten@users.noreply.github.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-06T17:57:21Z",
