          "id": "4f143f4c7147a4d910aede68fe839f4751c1b34d",
          "message": "[confmap/provider/httpprovider] Honor retrieval context (#16374)\n\n#### Description\n\nMake HTTP and HTTPS config retrieval respect the caller's context, so a\nstalled config server no longer blocks after cancellation or a deadline.\n\n#### Link to tracking issue\n\nFixes #16351\n\n#### Testing\n\nAdded deadline and cancellation tests for both HTTP and HTTPS. They fail\nbefore the fix and pass after it.\n\nThe affected module suites pass with race detection and FIPS mode\nenabled. Non-FIPS TLS tests, formatting, lint, and changelog validation\nalso pass.\n\n#### Documentation\n\nAdded a changelog entry.\n\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Antonio Jimenez <antonjim@thousandEyes.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-13T12:11:36Z",
          "tree_id": "8333daee159092bede6e1b724f9dc7c0ba427c9a",
