          "id": "d2383c4ed1521969f732672f44b9418f702dfa0d",
          "message": "[chore] [cmd/builder] Document connectors, excludes, build_tags, and resource in README (#16405)\n\n#### Description\n\nUpdates the `## Configuration` section in `cmd/builder/README.md` to\ndocument supported options that were previously missing from the\ndocumentation:\n- Added `connectors` to the list of top-level module types and added an\nexample in the sample manifest.\n- Documented `excludes` directives alongside `replaces` in both the\nexplanation text and the sample manifest.\n- Documented `dist.build_tags` for passing custom Go build tags during\nbinary compilation, and `dist.resource`\n(`dist.resource.detection.detectors`) for controlling which resource\ndetectors are compiled into the binary.\n\n#### Link to tracking issue\n\nFixes #16366\n\n#### Testing\n\nDocumentation-only change. Verified markdown formatting and syntax.\n\n#### Documentation\n\nUpdated `cmd/builder/README.md` in the `## Configuration` section.\n\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\nSigned-off-by: Yash Verma <yashraj.dns@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Alex Boten <223565+codeboten@users.noreply.github.com>",
