          "id": "06b3e8ad2c71492544a68bacc59e831a70995218",
          "message": "[chore][receiver/otlp] Correct profiles endpoint documentation (#16432)\n\n#### Description\n\nThe README documented profiles_url_path, but that configuration option\ndoes not exist. Profiles are served at /v1development/profiles path.\nThis PR removes the incorrect configuration as per the suggested fix. It\ndoes not change receiver runtime behaviour or make the profile path\nconfigurable.\n\n#### Link to tracking issue\n\nFixes #16353\n\n#### Testing\n\nI ran go test ./... from receiver/otlpreceiver and it passed. I also ran\nmake markdownlint from the repository root and it passed. I have\nconfirmed that profiles_url_path no longer appears under\nreceiver/otlpreceiver. No new automated tests were needed because this\nchanges the documentation and removes an unused fixture.\n\n#### Documentation\n\nThe README correctly explains that profiles use the fixed\n/v1development/profiles endpoint and that the configuration option was\nremoved.\n\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: wildchaser1703 <53348090+wildchaser1703@users.noreply.github.com>",
