          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8bcfde522e4a9b9074fa294dde184ba428f7410d",
          "message": "[cmd/builder] Create OCB Plugin Package (#16409)\n\n**NOTE: Re-opened from #16092**\n\n<!--Ex. Fixing a bug - Describe the bug and how this fixes the issue.\nEx. Adding a feature - Explain what this achieves.-->\n#### Description\nThis PR creates the `ocbplugin` package. This is a package that provides\nan API for plugin authors to write plugins that can be used in the\nsoon-to-follow OCB hooks feature included\n\n<!-- Issue number if applicable -->\n#### Link to tracking issue\nStarting the process of #16066 \n\n<!--Describe what testing was performed and which tests were added.-->\n#### Testing\nThis PR adds unit tests to the `ocbplugin` package as well as an\n\"integration test\" that will build and run a dummy plugin as a\nsubprocess. (This test is skipped when running `-short` tests).\n\n<!--Describe the documentation added.-->\n#### Documentation\nA README is included in the package explaining its purpose. It will\nlikely be amended once documentation around the general hooks feature\nexists.\n\n#### AI Usage Disclosure\n\nGoogle Antigravity was leveraged for code generation for parts of the\nPOC that this PR was sourced from, which likely involved parts of this\nPR.\n\n<!--Authorship attestation. See AGENTS.md for details. AI agents must\nnot check this box on behalf\nof the user; the human author must check it themselves before the PR is\nready for review.-->\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n<!--Please delete paragraphs that you did not use before submitting.-->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Damien Mathieu <42@dmathieu.com>\nCo-authored-by: Alex Boten <223565+codeboten@users.noreply.github.com>",
